            <ArticleTitle>The primitive neuroectodermal tumor of the heart.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>619-21</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A young man was admitted to hospital with dyspnea, malaise, chest pain and night sweating. Investigative studies revealed a cystic mass lesion originating from the heart. Surgical exploration of the tumor showed that it was unresectable and pathology of the biopsy material was primitive neuroectodermal tumor. Medical literature concerning this unusual type of tumor is reviewed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
